Python Data Types:
🚀 Python Basics – Data Types
In Python, everything is an object, and data types define what kind of value a variable holds.
🔹 Built-in Data Types in Python:
 1️⃣ Numeric → int, float, complex
 2️⃣ Sequence → list, tuple, range
 3️⃣ Text → str
 4️⃣ Mapping → dict
 5️⃣ Set → set, frozenset
 6️⃣ Boolean → bool
 7️⃣ Binary → bytes, bytearray, memoryview
 8️⃣ None → NoneType
📌 Example:

x = 10        # int
y = 3.14      # float
z = "Hello"   # str
a = [1,2,3]   # list
b = (4,5,6)   # tuple
c = {"name":"Shiva", "role":"DevOps"}  # dict
💡 Key takeaway: Python is dynamically typed — you don’t declare the type, Python decides it automatically at runtime.
👉 Understanding Data Types + Operators together forms the foundation of Python programming.
